{"nodes": [{"id": "specs_2026_08_19_ai_grounded_context_design_spec", "label": "Spec: AI Grounded Context and Injection Defence", "file_type": "document", "source_file": "docs/superpowers/specs/2026-08-19-ai-grounded-context-design.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "specs_2026_08_19_ai_grounded_context_design_prompt_injection_defence", "label": "Prompt Injection Defence by Construction", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/superpowers/specs/2026-08-19-ai-grounded-context-design.md", "source_location": "## \u0413\u043e\u043b\u043e\u0432\u043d\u0438\u0439 \u0456\u043d\u0432\u0430\u0440\u0456\u0430\u043d\u0442", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Client-written questionnaire fields (pet name, breed string, allergies, behaviour notes) are stored forever and could contain 'ignore previous instructions'. Instead of filtering them, the breed is used only as a Python-side lookup key into the Altegio catalog; the model only ever sees admin-written service titles (which already encode the breed) and numeric weight. The injection surface disappears by construction rather than by filter, at the accepted UX cost that the bot says 'for your Yorkie' instead of 'for Barney'."}, {"id": "specs_2026_08_19_ai_grounded_context_design_amount_validation", "label": "Deterministic Amount Validation of Model Output", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/superpowers/specs/2026-08-19-ai-grounded-context-design.md", "source_location": "## \u0414\u0435\u0442\u0435\u0440\u043c\u0456\u043d\u043e\u0432\u0430\u043d\u0456 \u043f\u0435\u0440\u0435\u0432\u0456\u0440\u043a\u0438 \u0432\u0456\u0434\u043f\u043e\u0432\u0456\u0434\u0456", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Prompt rules are bypassable and are explicitly not a security boundary; the boundary is this post-check. Every hryvnia amount in the reply is regex-extracted, normalised (spaces, NBSP, commas, prefix/suffix currency, UAH) and compared numerically against AiContext.amounts, which contains every number that actually went into the context block including the range bounds. A single unknown amount replaces the whole reply with a deterministic price list. It is a post-check: Groq has already been called, only the display is suppressed. Known limit: amounts written as words are not caught, judged disproportionate to parse."}, {"id": "specs_2026_08_19_ai_grounded_context_design_price_total_ban", "label": "Ban on Price Totals", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/superpowers/specs/2026-08-19-ai-grounded-context-design.md", "source_location": "**\u041f\u0456\u0434\u0441\u0443\u043c\u043a\u0438 \u0437\u0430\u0431\u043e\u0440\u043e\u043d\u0435\u043d\u0456.**", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "A sum of two real prices is not in the context, so the strict check would reject it anyway. Forbidding totals in the prompt was chosen over widening the check to pairwise sums (18 positions = 153 combinations), because widening weakens the single real guard. Non-technical reason too: the final amount is confirmed by the groomer on inspection, so a bot confidently saying 'together 1500' promises what it does not control."}, {"id": "specs_2026_08_19_ai_grounded_context_design_link_whitelist", "label": "Outbound Link Whitelist", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/superpowers/specs/2026-08-19-ai-grounded-context-design.md", "source_location": "**\u041f\u043e\u0441\u0438\u043b\u0430\u043d\u043d\u044f.**", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "The model has no internet, but data-borne text could still coax it into printing a foreign URL. Only the booking widget URL survives. Review round hardened this: host comparison via urllib.parse instead of startswith (so '?u=https://evil.com' and glued URLs no longer pass), plus a ban on a second scheme in the remainder, and whitespace is only renormalised when something was actually cut so newlines in ordinary replies survive."}, {"id": "specs_2026_08_19_ai_grounded_context_design_rate_limit", "label": "Per-User AI Rate Limit", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/superpowers/specs/2026-08-19-ai-grounded-context-design.md", "source_location": "## \u041b\u0456\u043c\u0456\u0442\u0438", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "15 messages per hour per tg_user_id on a sliding in-memory window. Protects the shared free Groq quota from a single user hammering the chat; on exceeding it Groq is not called at all (the only path where the model is skipped) and the client gets the same deterministic salon-phone text used for exhausted quota, so no third fallback wording is introduced."}, {"id": "specs_2026_08_19_ai_grounded_context_design_quota_digest", "label": "Groq Quota Digest at 18:30", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/superpowers/specs/2026-08-19-ai-grounded-context-design.md", "source_location": "### \u0414\u0430\u0439\u0434\u0436\u0435\u0441\u0442 \u043f\u043e\u0441\u0442\u0440\u0430\u0436\u0434\u0430\u043b\u0438\u0445 \u043a\u043b\u0456\u0454\u043d\u0442\u0456\u0432 \u043e 18:30", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "A daily gate fired at the first 429 would list exactly one affected client and never mention anyone hit later that day, so 'list for the day' would in practice mean 'first victim'. A fixed-time digest lets the set accumulate. 18:30 sits right after the 18:00 booking-incomplete notice so admins process both lists at once in working hours; the minute component forces now.time() comparison instead of the project's usual now.hour. Sent through the synchronous notify_admins because the cron path deliberately bypasses the event loop. Accepted limits: the owner learns at 18:30 rather than immediately, and a process restart loses the in-memory set."}, {"id": "specs_2026_08_19_ai_grounded_context_design_catalog_cache", "label": "In-Process Catalog Cache with Stale Fallback", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/superpowers/specs/2026-08-19-ai-grounded-context-design.md", "source_location": "## \u041c\u043e\u0434\u0443\u043b\u0456", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Catalog TTL one hour, branch directory one day, kept in process memory on purpose: the alternative (a daily Supabase snapshot) means a new table, a new migration, a new BACKUP_TABLES row and up-to-a-day staleness for data that changes a few times a year. On Altegio failure the expired entry is served anyway with a WARNING \u2014 an old price list beats no prices, accepted at the cost that withdrawn services can be quoted for a long time with no signal other than the log line."}, {"id": "specs_2026_08_19_ai_grounded_context_design_client_isolation", "label": "Client Isolation by Telegram User ID", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/superpowers/specs/2026-08-19-ai-grounded-context-design.md", "source_location": "## \u0406\u0437\u043e\u043b\u044f\u0446\u0456\u044f \u043a\u043b\u0456\u0454\u043d\u0442\u0456\u0432", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Context is built solely from the tg_user_id supplied by Telegram; no client identifier is ever accepted from message text, so one client's data cannot surface in another's conversation."}, {"id": "specs_2026_08_19_ai_grounded_context_design_trusted_source_sanitization", "label": "Sanitisation of the Trusted Source", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/superpowers/specs/2026-08-19-ai-grounded-context-design.md", "source_location": "## \u0421\u0430\u043d\u0456\u0442\u0438\u0437\u0430\u0446\u0456\u044f \u0434\u043e\u0432\u0456\u0440\u0435\u043d\u043e\u0433\u043e \u0434\u0436\u0435\u0440\u0435\u043b\u0430", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Service titles and addresses are written by salon admins in Altegio \u2014 not hostile input, but not sterile either. Each value is flattened, truncated to 120 chars and stripped of the '===' sequence that delimits the data block, so a title cannot close the block and start issuing instructions. A review round rejected an interim blacklist of phrases ('\u041a\u0406\u041d\u0415\u0426\u042c \u0414\u0410\u041d\u0418\u0425', '\u0414\u0410\u041d\u0406 \u0421\u0410\u041b\u041e\u041d\u0423') as unscalable: removing '===' alone already makes a full boundary marker unforgeable."}, {"id": "specs_2026_08_19_ai_grounded_context_design_graceful_degradation", "label": "Graceful Degradation of Context Assembly", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/superpowers/specs/2026-08-19-ai-grounded-context-design.md", "source_location": "## \u0414\u0435\u0433\u0440\u0430\u0434\u0430\u0446\u0456\u044f", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Context assembly may never break the chat, because AI is the fallback for everything the client types. Altegio down with cache -> stale cache; without cache -> context with no prices; Supabase down -> client treated as unregistered; any other error -> base prompt with no context; Groq 429 -> phone text plus digest; other Groq error -> apology."}, {"id": "specs_2026_08_19_ai_grounded_context_design_guard_trip_counter", "label": "Guard Trip Visibility Counter", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/superpowers/specs/2026-08-19-ai-grounded-context-design.md", "source_location": "## \u0412\u0438\u0434\u0438\u043c\u0456\u0441\u0442\u044c \u0441\u043f\u0440\u0430\u0446\u044e\u0432\u0430\u043d\u044c", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Catches the scenario where Groq swaps the model or the prompt drifts and the bot silently enters permanent-fallback mode: such a break produces a steady stream of rejections, so five in an hour raises one admin alert, at most hourly. Same principle as the backup module \u2014 a silent failure is worse than a loud one. Review corrected the docstring claim that the counter survives a restart: in-memory state does not, the threshold simply refills."}, {"id": "specs_2026_08_19_ai_grounded_context_design_history_limit", "label": "Chat History Trimming", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/superpowers/specs/2026-08-19-ai-grounded-context-design.md", "source_location": "## \u041b\u0456\u043c\u0456\u0442\u0438", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "History previously grew until process restart, dragging tokens and latency; trimmed to the last 10 messages (about five exchanges). A fix round added that the window must not start with a leading assistant message, otherwise the model receives an answer to a question it cannot see. On any Groq error the unanswered user message is popped so the user/assistant pairing stays consistent."}], "edges": [{"source": "specs_2026_08_19_ai_grounded_context_design_spec", "target": "services_ai_context_build_context", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/superpowers/specs/2026-08-19-ai-grounded-context-design.md", "source_location": "\u041c\u043e\u0434\u0443\u043b\u0456", "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "specs_2026_08_19_ai_grounded_context_design_spec", "target": "services_ai_context_for_user", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/superpowers/specs/2026-08-19-ai-grounded-context-design.md", "source_location": "\u041c\u043e\u0434\u0443\u043b\u0456", "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "specs_2026_08_19_ai_grounded_context_design_spec", "target": "handlers_ai_chat_handle_message", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "so